# Known-debt ratchet for the samples gate. EMPTY = no known debt: every failure is a NEW failure.
# It may only shrink — an entry whose check starts passing is STALE and fails the run.
#
# Emptied 2026-08-25 (#1786). It was seeded with eight entries; all eight are now gone, for two
# different reasons that are worth keeping apart:
#   * FutuRe/{AmericasIns,AsiaRe,EuropeRe}/{LineOfBusiness,TransactionMapping} — retired as
#     NodeTypes by b63fbf057 (they are Markdown nodes now), so their entries named a scope the
#     gate no longer reports on. That reads as `Unverifiable`, which is WARNED and never failed —
#     i.e. six lines that could sit here for ever describing debt that no longer exists.
#   * Northwind/AnalyticsCatalog — DashboardLayoutAreas referenced four classes by their old
#     `*Views` names (`OrderViews`, `SalesViews`, `SupplierViews`, `ProductViews`); the real
#     classes are `*LayoutAreas`.
#   * Northwind/Product — ProductContent's `[Dimension(typeof(Supplier))]` / `typeof(Category)`
#     name records that live in Northwind/AnalyticsCatalog/Source, which the default source query
#     (`namespace:<node>/Source scope:subtree`) cannot reach; Product.json now declares the two
#     `shared=@…` sources entries that pull exactly those two files in.
#
# NOT emptied: the two PensionFund entries below were added AFTER this branch's base
# (#2250) and are untouched by #1786's work. They are real, live debt — see each.

# ── PensionFund: revealed by #2063, NOT caused by it ────────────────────────────────────────────
# PensionFund ships 72 files, 62 of them BOM'd, including all 5 of its NodeTypes. Until #2063 the
# gate's own discovery parsed package bytes raw and dropped every BOM'd file, so this package
# gated `0 type(s)` and reported [PASS] over nothing. Both entries below are pre-existing debt that
# was simply never looked at — each diagnosed, neither bulk-added.

# PensionFund/BalanceSheet — the legacy scope-generator `#r` cannot resolve on a gate/deploy host.
# BalanceSheetScopes.cs:20 declares `#r "nuget:MeshWeaver.BusinessRules.Generator"`.
# GeneratorPipeline.StripBuiltInScopeGeneratorRef removes that directive from the NuGet resolve set
# ONLY when `BuiltInGeneratorPaths` is non-empty, i.e. when MeshWeaver.BusinessRules.Generator.dll
# sits beside the app. BusinessRules left the platform (f7a8c086c — it ships in the
# MeshWeaver.Plugins/BusinessRules plugin), so that list is EMPTY on this host and the strip is a
# no-op. The directive then reaches NuGet, where NuGet.config's packageSourceMapping pins
# `MeshWeaver.*` exclusively to the `mesh-local` source `dist/packages` — a feed #395 stopped
# producing (dotnet-test.yml:372-377 documents that CI deliberately packs it no longer). Result:
# NuGet.Protocol.FatalProtocolException "The local source '<repo>/dist/packages' doesn't exist".
# Deterministic, not a flake: no `dist/packages` on any CI runner and no generator dll beside
# mw-plugin-test. The real fix is content-side (drop the legacy `#r`; the generator is supplied via
# `shared=@BusinessRules/Scope/Source`) and is NOT part of #2063 — it needs the plugin's scope
# generator to be reachable from the gate host, which is a separate change.
PensionFund/BalanceSheet compile

# PensionFund idempotence — INTERMITTENT known debt. Do not remove on a single green run.
# Removed once tonight because the gate reported it STALE ("now passing"); the very next run
# reported it as a NEW failure. Both readings are correct — the check is nondeterministic,
# because whether it fires depends on whether the Currency NodeType has COMPILED yet.
#
# The underlying defect is real and is tracked separately: the second install rewrites
# Currency/{CHF,EUR,USD}. `Currency.DecimalPlaces` carries a C# initializer `= 2` and all
# three instance files author `"decimalPlaces": 2`. Once the NodeType compiles, its content
# type is registered, the installer materialises a typed `Currency` and re-serialises it, and
# default-suppression drops the property whose value equals the type's default. The stored
# node then differs from the authored file and the unchanged-skip misses.
PensionFund idempotence
